00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:09.000 align:start position:0%
the Devon building control partnership  is a shared service across three  authorities we check all types of  building works across the district's to  make sure it meets reasonable standards  contained in the building regulations  which are produced and regularly updated  by central government our surveyors  ensure the health and safety of people  in and about buildings we check that  they are structurally sound and will not  fall down we make sure there are  suitable fire precautions for example  fire escapes and a system of smoke  detection we make sure there is  reasonable access for all people with  disabilities the sick the young and the  old we look for buildings to be  sustainable and thermally efficient and  encourage reduced energy usage in order  to limit the production of co2 one of  the primary causes of climate change the  costs are made against the individuals  for their applications and do not come  from council tax building control also  deal with the council's responsibility  for dangerous structures for example  when there has been a fire or other  catastrophic event which may lead to  buildings becoming unstable by the way  we don't do planning permissions
 

